'''Bhadradri Kothagudem district''' is a [[List of districts in India|district]] in the east of the [[Indian state]] of [[Telangana]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Names of 6 new districts changed|url=https://www.thehindu.com/todays-paper/tp-national/tp-telangana/Names-of-6-new-districts-changed/article15660997.ece|access-date=4 November 2016|work=The Hindu|date=22 October 2016|language=en-IN}}</ref> [[Kothagudem]] is the district headquarters.<ref name="profile"> Bhandaradri kothagudem district is located in eastern part of Telangana.{{Cite web|url=http://www.trac.telangana.gov.in/New_Districts/districts/02-Bhadradri-Kothagudem.pdf|title=Bhadradri-Kothagudem district|website=Official website of Medchal district|access-date=29 June 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170110191528/http://trac.telangana.gov.in/New_Districts/districts/02-Bhadradri-Kothagudem.pdf|archive-date=10 January 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref> It is the largest district in Telangana, with an area of 7483&nbsp;km<sup>2</sup>.<ref name=":0" /> It borders the districts [[Khammam district|Khammam]], [[Mahabubabad district|Mahabubabad]], [[Mulugu district|Mulugu]] and shares a boundary with the bordering states [[Chhattisgarh]] and [[Andhra Pradesh]]. The district comprises 24 [[mandal]]s and 2 [[revenue division]]s, [[Kothagudem]] and [[Bhadrachalam]], and 481 [[gram panchayat]]s, and 5 [[municipalities]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://kothagudem.telangana.gov.in/?|title=BHADRADRI KOTHAGUDEM DISTRICT|website=Kothagudem.telangana.gov.in|access-date=3 August 2026}}</ref>

Kothagudem district contains some major industries, and is endowed with a variety of important minerals such as [[coal]]. The [[Singareni Collieries Company]] (SCCL), a government coal mining company jointly owned by the [[Government of Telangana]] and [[Government of India]], has its headquarters in Kothagudem. SCCL operates 16 [[opencast]] and 30 underground mines in four districts of Telangana with a manpower of around 58,837.{{When|date=March 2024}} 

[[Kothagudem Thermal Power Station]], which is located in [[Palvancha]], is one of the coal-based power plants of [[Telangana State Power Generation Corporation Limited]]. The Paperboards and Specialty Papers Division of [[ITC Limited]] (ITC-PSPD) is located at [[Sarapaka|Sarapaka village]] near Bhadrachalam.

== History ==
Prehistoric man probably roamed around the areas of lower Godavari valley<ref>{{cite book|title=Paleolithic History of Godavari valley|url =https://books.google.com/books?id=OBJuAAAAMAAJ&q=Bhadrachalam|year =1984}}</ref> in the surroundings of [[Bhadrachalam]], [[Kothagudem]], [[Pinapaka mandal|Pinapaka]] and [[Paloncha]] Taluks in the district.

Megalithic Dolmens were found at Janampet of Pinapaka Taluk.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://asihyd.ap.nic.in/khammam.html|title=Archeological Survey of India}}</ref> and Padugonigudem<ref>{{cite news| url=http://www.hindu.com/2011/04/22/stories/2011042263190600.htm | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110426083135/http://www.hindu.com/2011/04/22/stories/2011042263190600.htm | url-status=dead | archive-date=2011-04-26 | location=Chennai, India | work=[[The Hindu]] | title=3,000-year-old megalithic site discovered in Khammam | date=2011-04-22}}</ref> villages in Gundala Taluk of the district were rich in Megalithic cultural remnants explored and discovered recently.

Buddhist sites in the district are found at [[Aswaraopeta]] and Karukonda<ref>{{Cite web| url=http://www.aparchaeologymuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/05/Khammam-dt.pdf | title=Khammam district | access-date=2013-05-02 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140203152357/http://www.aparchaeologymuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/05/Khammam-dt.pdf | archive-date=2014-02-03 | url-status=dead}}</ref> near [[Kothagudem]].

Bhadrachalam town has a documented history of a [[Sita Ramachandraswamy Temple, Bhadrachalam|Rama Temple]] constructed  around 17th century CE by [[Kancherla Gopanna]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bhadrachalarama.org/templehistory.html|title= Welcome to Bhadrachala Sree Seetha Ramachandra swamy temple|work=bhadrachalarama.org}}</ref> popularly known as Bhakta Ramadasu or Bhadrachala Ramadasu is a saint-poet.

== Geography ==

Bhadradri Kothagudem is the easternmost district of [[Telangana]] and is spread over an area of {{convert|7483|km2|sqmi|abbr=on}}.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=TSDPS |title=Telangana State Development and Planning Society |url=https://www.tsdps.telangana.gov.in/Atlas.pdf}}</ref> The district is bounded on the north and northeast by the [[Bijapur district, Chhattisgarh|Bijapur]] and [[Sukma district|Sukma]] districts of [[Chhattisgarh]], on the east by [[Polavaram district]] of [[Andhra Pradesh]], on the south and southeast by the [[Khammam district|Khammam]] and on southeast by [[Eluru district|Eluru]] of [[Andhra Pradesh]] , on the west by [[Mahabubabad district]] and on the northwest by [[Mulugu district]].

The district contains [[Kinnerasani Wildlife Sanctuary]] and also rich in forest reserves.

