== Administrative divisions ==
[[File:Bhadradri District basic outline map.png|thumb|240px|Bhadradri Kothagudem district outline map]]
The district has two [[List of revenue divisions in Telangana|revenue divisions]] of [[Bhadrachalam]] and [[Kothagudem]] and is sub-divided into 23 [[mandal]]s.<ref name="profile" /> Ankit is the present [[District magistrate|collector]] of the district, having assumed the role in 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |title=District Officials |url=https://www.telangana.gov.in/contacts/district-officials |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230923164520/https://www.telangana.gov.in/contacts/district-officials |archive-date=23 September 2023 |access-date=20 January 2024 |website=Telangana State Portal}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=15 July 2023 |title=Mr.Ankit has taken charge as Collector and District Magistrate from Mr.Jitesh V Patil.|url=https://telanganatoday.com/dr-priyanka-ala-takes-charge-as-kothagudem-collector |access-date=20 January 2024 |work=[[Telangana Today]]}}</ref>

=== Constituencies ===
The district contains five [[Telangana Legislative Assembly]] constituencies. [[Kothagudem Assembly constituency]] includes the towns of Kothagudem and [[Palvancha]],  part of the [[Khammam Lok Sabha constituency]]. [[Aswaraopeta Assembly constituency]] is a Scheduled Tribe (ST) reserved constituency, and is also part of the [[Khammam Lok Sabha constituency]]. The [[Bhadrachalam Assembly constituency|Bhadrachalam]], [[Yellandu Assembly constituency|Yellandu]], and [[Pinapaka Assembly constituency|Pinapaka Assembly constituencies]] are ST reserved constituencies, and are part of the [[Mahabubabad Lok Sabha constituency]].

